{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":154248,"num_turns":4,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"486e9ca4-2287-4ac3-a9f7-651c8afe33c7","total_cost_usd":0.8416485,"usage":{"input_tokens":48,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42184,"cache_read_input_tokens":138253,"output_tokens":13064,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42184,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9335,"cache_read_input_tokens":60662,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2176},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":23762,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.023842,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":48,"outputTokens":13064,"cacheReadInputTokens":138253,"cacheCreationInputTokens":42184,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8178065000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"debris-designer\",\n  \"size_classes\": {\n    \"small\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 1,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 2,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": true,\n      \"fragile_uncrushable\": true\n    },\n    \"medium\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 2,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 4,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": true,\n      \"fragile_uncrushable\": true\n    },\n    \"oversized\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 6,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 12,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": false,\n      \"fragile_uncrushable\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"debris\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"torn_foil_blanket\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Torn Foil Blanket\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 52500,\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 5.5,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A shredded sheet of multi-layer insulation that weighs nothing and tears if you look at it wrong — the cheapest way to meet the fragile flag on your first launch.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"crumpled_panel_stack\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Crumpled Panel Stack\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 56000,\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 8,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 18,\n      \"notes\": \"Bus panels folded together by the cascade; the commonest thing in the low envelope and the piece a break-even run is built out of.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_solar_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Solar Array\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 61500,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 10.5,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"Half a wing of shattered cells still on its hinge — light for its bulk, and the glass goes if the shield does.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"bent_truss_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Bent Truss Section\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 67000,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 13,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 15,\n      \"notes\": \"Structural spine off a comms bus, kinked but sound; four slots uncrushed makes it the first real hold-space decision.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"spent_kick_motor_casing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Spent Kick Motor Casing\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 73500,\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 15.5,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 12,\n      \"notes\": \"An expended apogee motor, burnt through and empty — dense scrap steel in one tidy slot.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"collapsed_dish_frame\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Collapsed Dish Frame\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 86500,\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 48,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A folded ten-metre reflector rib cage — the magnet skids off it; crane cable only, so the shipping slice sees it and cannot have it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shredded_antenna_mesh\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Shredded Antenna Mesh\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 93000,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 19,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"Gold-plated wire mesh balled up around its former spar; worth real money by mass and it will not survive a hard flare.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_battery_pallet\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Battery Pallet\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 99500,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 22.5,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"A vented nickel-hydrogen pack on its mounting rails — heavy for the low band and the first piece that makes you check the mass dial.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"seized_reaction_wheel_housing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Seized Reaction Wheel Housing\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 106000,\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 25,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 12,\n      \"notes\": \"A momentum wheel welded solid by its own bearing failure; a whole lot of dense metal in a single slot.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"burst_pressurant_sphere\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Burst Pressurant Sphere\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 113000,\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 27,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A titanium helium bottle split along its weld — the densest single-slot grab available to a starter hold.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"delaminated_radiator_fin\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Delaminated Radiator Fin\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 120000,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 24,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A heat-pipe panel peeling apart at the bondline; four slots, glass-brittle, and the last fragile piece before the shipping slice gets serious.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"torn_solar_wing_spar\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Torn Solar Wing Spar\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 131000,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 34,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"The carbon backbone of a full array wing, cells stripped away — the bread-and-butter mid-envelope haul.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_optics_barrel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Optics Barrel\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 138000,\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 30,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"An imager tube with its primary mirror starred through; one slot, high value per kilo, and its uncrushable flag is now a field rather than a sentence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fractured_docking_collar\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Fractured Docking Collar\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 145000,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 41,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A berthing ring sheared off its tunnel — forged alloy, awkward shape, and no argument about whether it is worth the trip.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dead_thruster_quad\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Dead Thruster Quad\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 152500,\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 45,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 12,\n      \"notes\": \"Four RCS nozzles on a common manifold, valves fused shut; the best mass-per-slot in the middle third.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"buckled_pressure_bulkhead\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Buckled Pressure Bulkhead\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 160000,\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 96,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A crew-module end dome caved in on itself — crane cable only, and a standing advertisement for the hold you cannot afford yet.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ruptured_helium_tank\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Ruptured Helium Tank\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 167000,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 52,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"A composite-overwrapped bottle blown open at the boss; heavy, sturdy, and it eats four slots uncrushed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shattered_star_tracker\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Shattered Star Tracker\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 174000,\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 48,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"Navigation optics in a machined housing, baffle crushed — dense, delicate, and the piece that teaches you to deploy the chute early.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"warped_gyro_deck\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Warped Gyro Deck\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 181500,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 61,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"A whole attitude-control tray, three wheels still bolted down — a single grab that fills a starter hold's mass budget by itself.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_ablative_nose_cone\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Ablative Nose Cone\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 189000,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 58,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A charred fairing tip off an upper stage, its ablator crazed through — ironic cargo, and it burns first when the shield goes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"split_avionics_rack\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Split Avionics Rack\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 197500,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 64,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A flight computer bay cracked open, boards still seated; the richest fragile piece below the top third and a genuine gamble on your flying.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"torn_reactor_shield_plate\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Torn Reactor Shield Plate\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 209000,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 82,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"Tungsten-laced shadow shielding off a nuclear tug — the top third's baseline haul, and it doubles your reentry problem on its own.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_deep_space_dish\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Deep Space Dish\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 217500,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 78,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A precision high-gain reflector, its face split across the rim — enormous value and no tolerance for a late chute.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fused_ion_grid_assembly\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Fused Ion Grid Assembly\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 226000,\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 88,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"Molybdenum accelerator grids arced together into a solid brick; one slot, brutal mass, and half durability the whole way down.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"severed_boom_mast\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Severed Boom Mast\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 234000,\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 165,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"Thirty metres of deployable truss, sheared at the root — crane cable only, and the heaviest ordinary object in the envelope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scorched_fuel_cell_stack\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Scorched Fuel Cell Stack\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 242500,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 104,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"A platinum-catalysed cell stack off a crewed vehicle, casing scorched through — the top third's honest workhorse.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shattered_cryo_dewar\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Shattered Cryo Dewar\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 251000,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 98,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A vacuum-jacketed helium dewar with its inner vessel collapsed; heavy, fragile, and worth the whole trip if it lands intact.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"impact_pitted_engine_bell\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Impact Pitted Engine Bell\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 259500,\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 122,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 7,\n      \"notes\": \"A regeneratively cooled nozzle peppered by the cascade — the heaviest thing a hand magnet can legally take home.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_command_module_hatch\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Command Module Hatch\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 268000,\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 112,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A crew hatch with its pane starred, hanging just under the module — the last thing you pass on the way to Armstrong's prize, and a real temptation to overload.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"armstrongs_module\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Armstrong's Service Module\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 277000,\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"uncrushable\": true,\n      \"fixed_objective\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 3600,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"Apollo-era service module hanging at the ceiling, older than the cascade and still whole — one slot, roughly double the ship's mass, and the only object in the catalog that degrades pristine to damaged to scrap instead of breaking. fixed_objective true: it is placed, never rolled, and no weighted sampler may draw it.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"band_summary\": [\n    {\n      \"sample\": \"bottom\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 88333,\n      \"piece_count\": 11,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.1011,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 19.82\n    },\n    {\n      \"sample\": \"middle\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 165000,\n      \"piece_count\": 10,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.1739,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 52.9\n    },\n    {\n      \"sample\": \"top\",\n      \"altitude_m\": 241667,\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.25,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 494.33\n    }\n  ],\n  \"revision_notes\": [\n    \"Auditor finding fragile_never_crushable_and_premium_holds: fixed by taking the auditor's second suggested direction — an explicit field the fragile flag sets — rather than the first. Every debris entry now carries an uncrushable boolean, true on exactly the twelve fragile pieces and on armstrongs_module, false on every solid ordinary piece, and each size class carries fragile_uncrushable true so the exemption is stated in both places the auditor looked. With cargo.compactor_tier = 1 live, a compactor may now apply slots_crushed only to entries whose uncrushable is false; the twelve fragile ids the audit listed all read uncrushable true and take their uncrushed slot count at every tier. This is a field, not a note, and it is machine-checkable per piece.\",\n    \"I did not take the first suggested direction — dropping slots_crushed/slots_uncrushed from size_classes — because my charter fixes those numbers verbatim ('emit them as given; you are not tuning them') and the schema requires all three keys on every class. Deleting them would put the catalog outside its own contract to fix a rule that an added field fixes exactly. See design_notes for what the slot table means in the shipping slice.\",\n    \"Balancer concern 3, armstrongs_module spawn_weight: addressed without changing the weight. The charter and the schema both floor spawn_weight at 1, so 1 is the only legal value; the fix the balancer actually asked for is a flag, and armstrongs_module now carries fixed_objective true. Any sampler must filter entries carrying fixed_objective before it normalises weights. No other entry carries the field.\",\n    \"Balancer concern 4, the slot table: answered in design_notes rather than by editing masses. The table is complete-catalog bookkeeping, not shipping-slice behaviour — base_slots = 7 as seven pieces is correct and no mass figure in this file needs a crush factor applied.\",\n    \"Balancer concerns 1 and 2 I believe are misapplied; both are argued in design_notes and neither changed a piece. No mass, altitude, size class, spawn weight or id moved in this revision. band_summary is recomputed from the array as it now stands: the bottom third's fragile fraction is 9/89 = 0.1011, not the 0.1 previously reported off a weight sum of 90 — an arithmetic slip in the old summary, corrected here. Middle 12/69 = 0.1739 and top 10/40 = 0.25 recompute unchanged.\"\n  ],\n  \"design_notes\": [\n    \"On the balancer's concern that the floor population cannot make the full-hold-doubling rule true: I agree with the diagnosis and disagree with the proposed fix. Raising the bottom third's masses by a factor of five would put a shredded insulation blanket at 27 kg and a folded panel stack at 40 kg — heavier than the mid-band docking collar — which destroys the one property my charter calls central, that mass rises smoothly with altitude so a better haul is a harder ride home. It would also flatten the top-to-bottom mass factor from 5.4 to about 1.1 and delete the difficulty curve the catalog exists to carry. The doubling is a top-of-band property and always was: the GDD's own flown figure of ~1,398 kg for a full hold is a top-third hold, and the balancer reproduced it from the top third's 106.1 kg ordinary mean. A hold of floor scrap weighing 139 kg is not a broken catalog, it is what a first-launch haul of shredded foil should weigh — the rule wants restating as a property of a full hold at the top of the band, which is where the design's reentry problem lives.\",\n    \"On the balancer's concern that the three oversized pieces price something unreachable: they are correct that no oversized piece can enter a hold in the shipping slice, and that is deliberate and charter-mandated — one or two per third, marked hand_tetherable false, present so the catalog is complete and so the player meets the crane-cable limit as a visible rule about the tool at 86,500 m. Demoting them to medium would make the collapsed dish frame and the boom mast hand-tetherable, which is a scope change GDD 4.3 explicitly cut, and it would hand the player a 165 kg grab the magnet was never meant to take. The unreachable price is an economy artifact, not a catalog defect: size_class_base_value's oversized entry should be read as pricing cut content, or dropped on the economy side. Nothing in the shipping slice ever reads it.\",\n    \"What the slot table means, since two agents have now asked: in the shipping slice every piece is one slot, per GDD 4.3, and base_slots = 7 correctly means seven pieces. slots_crushed and slots_uncrushed describe the compactor and size-class content that GDD 4.3 cut, and are emitted because the charter fixes them and the schema requires them — they are the catalog's record of what the classes would cost if that content ever returned. No mass figure in this file depends on a crush factor. If the compactor is ever restored, the uncrushable field added in this revision is what keeps the fragile population out of it.\",\n    \"Mass climbs monotonically with altitude across the whole envelope rather than in steps: 5.5 kg at the floor to 122 kg at the top of the hand-tetherable population, with every adjacent pair inside about 30% of each other so no player ever crosses an arbitrary cliff. Excluding Armstrong's module, the top third's mean piece is 106.1 kg against the bottom third's 19.8 kg — a factor of 5.4, which is the GDD's bet that a better haul is a harder ride home, made visible in the numbers.\",\n    \"The reported top-third mean_mass_kg of 494.33 is the plain average the charter asks for and it includes Armstrong's module at 3,600 kg, which is why it reads an order of magnitude above the middle third. The ordinary-piece figure is 106.1 kg. Anything downstream that reasons about hold mass should use the ordinary population; the module is a single fixed objective above the shipping slice, not a spawn the player packs alongside other cargo — and it now says so in a field.\",\n    \"Armstrong's module is authored explicitly rather than being approximated by the heaviest ordinary piece. The heaviest ordinary object is the severed boom mast at 165 kg and the heaviest hand-tetherable one is the engine bell at 122 kg, so the module stands 22x above anything else that can enter a hold. The endgame rule that the module cannot plunge is therefore measured against the win condition and not against a nose cone.\",\n    \"Fragile fractions are spawn-weighted, not counted, and they were recomputed after this revision: bottom 9/89 = 0.1011, middle 12/69 = 0.1739, top 10/40 = 0.250. The counts alone would read 4/11, 4/10 and 4/9 — an almost flat gradient — which is exactly the failure mode the charter names. The weights carry the gradient: fragile pieces are common enough to be met at the floor and common enough to be a real hazard at the ceiling.\",\n    \"Every size class and the fragile flag appear inside the shipping slice, the bottom two thirds. Small, medium and fragile all show up in the first 40 km of the band; the oversized class is met at 86,500 m as a collapsed dish frame the magnet visibly refuses, so the player learns the crane-cable limit early and reads it as a rule about the tool rather than a bug.\",\n    \"Oversized pieces number exactly one per third and their masses are set by their local altitude neighbourhood rather than by their bulk — 48, 96 and 165 kg. Size class is a volume-and-slot statement, not a mass statement, so the oversized entries do not distort the mass-versus-altitude trend they sit inside, and the catalog stays coherent if the crane magnet is ever restored to scope.\",\n    \"No piece is strictly dominant. Density and slot cost are deliberately anticorrelated: the small classes (kick motor casing, pressurant sphere, thruster quad, ion grid) buy mass efficiency per slot at the price of raw value, while the mediums (truss, spar, gyro deck, fuel cell stack) pay better per grab and cost four slots uncrushed. Fragile pieces are the high-value-per-kilo end of both classes, so reaching for one is always a bet on the landing rather than a free upgrade — and with uncrushable now explicit, that bet can never be bought off by a compactor tier.\",\n    \"Altitudes are spread on roughly 7 km centres across the full 50,000-280,000 m envelope and deliberately avoid the Researcher's three sample altitudes of 65,000, 115,000 and 215,000 m. The samples are where the sweep measures; a catalog that clustered there would be reintroducing three discrete bands under a continuous label.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":47057,"ttft_stream_ms":5030,"time_to_request_ms":437,"type":"result","duration_ms":154296,"uuid":"43dfaf54-c149-457c-a1ae-a61d3dcc12f2"}
